.TH MAPS-NDJSON-VIEWER 1 "23 September 2026" "maps-apps 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maps-ndjson-viewer \- query decoded MAPS NDJSON message logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maps-ndjson-viewer
.RI [ file-or-directory ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maps-ndjson-viewer
loads MAPS message-log NDJSON through embedded DuckDB, decodes Base64 opaqueData,
and exposes decoded JSON for SQL analysis. Directories are searched recursively.
.PP
An existing DuckDB database can be opened directly by supplying --database without an
input path. In that mode no log import is performed and the database must already exist.
.PP
The relations maps_log and mavlink_log are available to queries. No external database
server or DuckDB installation is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --topics
List topics and record counts.
.TP
.BI --sql " query"
Execute DuckDB SQL against maps_log or mavlink_log.
.TP
.B --interactive
Open the interactive SQL prompt, including when launched from an IDE.
.TP
.B "-ui, --ui"
Open the DuckDB UI in the default browser against the same embedded DuckDB instance.
The viewer remains running until it is terminated.
.TP
.B --mcp
Expose the loaded DuckDB data as a Model Context Protocol server over standard
input/output.
.TP
.B --mcp-http
Expose the same read-only MCP tools using Streamable HTTP at /mcp.
.TP
.BI --bind " address"
Bind address for --mcp-http. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
TCP port for --mcp-http. The default is 8090.
.TP
.BI --database " file"
Persist imported records in a DuckDB database file, or open an existing database when
no input path is supplied.
.TP
.BI --format " table|ndjson|csv|raw"
Select the result format. Raw output requires exactly one selected column and writes its
value directly without a result envelope.
.TP
.B --raw
Equivalent to --format raw.
.TP
.BI --output " file"
Write results to a file. A .csv suffix selects CSV; other suffixes select NDJSON unless
--format or --raw is specified.
.SH MCP
Both MCP transports provide list_relations, describe_relation, list_topics, and
query_sql. MCP SQL is read-only and DuckDB external access is disabled.
.PP
The HTTP transport has no application authentication or TLS. Keep it bound to loopback
unless access is protected by a firewall, VPN, SSH tunnel, or authenticated HTTPS
reverse proxy.
.SH EXAMPLES
Expose an existing database using stdio MCP:
.PP
.nf
maps-ndjson-viewer --database telemetry.duckdb --mcp
.fi
.PP
Expose an existing database using Streamable HTTP:
.PP
.nf
maps-ndjson-viewer --database telemetry.duckdb --mcp-http
.fi
.PP
Listen on all interfaces:
.PP
.nf
maps-ndjson-viewer --database telemetry.duckdb --mcp-http --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 8090
.fi
.PP
Open an existing database in the DuckDB UI:
.PP
.nf
maps-ndjson-viewer --database telemetry.duckdb -ui
.fi
.PP
Open an existing database and extract STANAG task requests as replayable JSONL payloads:
.PP
.nf
maps-ndjson-viewer --database telemetry.duckdb \
  --sql "SELECT payload FROM maps_log WHERE topic LIKE '%/MessageTypeEnum_TASK_ADMIN' ORDER BY receivedTimestamp" \
  --raw --output tasking.jsonl
.fi
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B .topics
List all topics.
.TP
.B .mavlink-topics
List MAVLink topics.
.TP
.B .schema
Describe maps_log.
.TP
.B .quit
Exit the interactive shell.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/maps/apps/ndjson_viewer.jar
Executable JAR installed by the maps-apps Debian package.
.SH AUTHOR
MapsMessaging B.V.
